[center][size=5][color=#e6b85c][b]TRAVELLERS REST PERFORMANCE DIAGNOSTIC[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[color=#00ff00][size=4][font=Arial Black][b]What it does[/b][/font][/size][/color]
[size=3]This is a [color=#ffff00]measuring tool[/color], not a [color=#ff0000]gameplay mod[/color]. It records how long your game takes to load, where it freezes, and whether memory keeps growing, then writes a plain text report you can read or send to a mod author.[/size]

It changes no gameplay and writes nothing into your saves. It counts, and it writes a file.

[size=4][b]Highlights[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#d9ead3]A small status panel in the corner[/color] shows what it is doing, so a long load is not mistaken for a hang. It can be moved or turned off.[/*]
[*][color=#d9ead3]Loading is measured automatically[/color]. No key to press, and nothing to miss.[/*]
[*][color=#d9ead3]It finds the freeze, not just the slow part[/color]. A freeze is recorded with the game's own log lines from the seconds before it, which usually names the cause.[/*]
[*][color=#d9ead3]It catches mods installed twice[/color]. A mod loaded twice runs twice, and that is a common cause of unexplained slowdown.[/*]
[*][color=#d9ead3]Memory growth over a session[/color], so a leak can be told apart from ordinary loading.[/*]
[*][color=#d9ead3]A readable report[/color] in English, ready to attach to a bug report.[/*]
[*][color=#d9ead3]Independent[/color] of every other mod. Install it alone, alongside others, or not at all.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]No keys, no menus[/b][/size]
There is nothing to press and nothing to configure before it works. Start the game, load a save, play as normal. The panel appears by itself and the report is written as it goes.

[size=4][b]What it found on my machine[/b][/size]
On this machine, loading a save takes about 21 seconds - and 13 of those seconds are a [b]single frozen frame[/b], not slow loading spread out. The report named the cause from the game's own log: the game tries to generate sprite outlines from a texture it cannot read, and retries 431 times in one load.

That is the kind of answer this is built to produce. It measures first, so the fix can be aimed at the right thing.

[size=4][b]Where the report goes[/b][/size]
The report is written to
[quote][b]BepInEx\TravellersRestProfiler\profiler-report-latest.txt[/b] [/quote]
and rewritten as the game runs, so it is always current. There is nothing to export and no file to hunt for.

[color=#f9cb9c][size=4][b]The status panel[/b][/size][/color]
The panel shows the current step, the elapsed time, how many loads have been measured and how many freezes recorded. It sits in the bottom-left corner by default, because that is the only corner Travellers Rest leaves empty: the top-left holds the clock and money, the top-right is where achievement notifications appear, and the bottom centre holds the hotbar.

If it covers something you want to see, move it rather than turning it off. [b]HudMargin[/b] sets the distance from the edge in pixels, and the corner is chosen with [b]HudOnLeft[/b] and [b]HudAtBottom[/b]. Setting [b]ShowHud[/b] to false gives a completely invisible mod.

[color=#ffd966][size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size][/color]
[list]
[*]Travellers Rest for Windows.[/*]
[*][url=https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx/releases/tag/v5.4.21]BepInEx 5.4.21 x64[/url], or a compatible BepInEx 5 installation.[/*]
[/list]

[color=#ffd966][size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size][/color]
[list=1]
[*]Install BepInEx in the folder containing [b]TravellersRest.exe[/b], then start the game once.[/*]
[*]Extract this archive into Travellers Rest's [b]Windows[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Start the game. The panel appears and the report starts being written.[/*]
[/list]

The archive extracts itself into
[quote] [b]BepInEx\plugins\TravellersRestProfiler[/b][/quote]
Nothing else is required.

[b]Settings[/b]
All settings live in
[quote][b]BepInEx\config\actepukc.travellersrest.profiler.cfg[/b][/quote]
and have sensible defaults.

[code]ReportIntervalSeconds[/code]
sets how often the report is rewritten, 20 seconds by default.
[code]StallThresholdMs[/code]
sets how long a frame must last to be recorded as a freeze; the default of 2000 ms is far beyond any legitimate frame.

[size=4][b]What it does not measure[/b][/size]
It does not attribute CPU time to individual mods. Doing that means patching every method of every installed plugin at runtime, and when that goes wrong it does not crash - it quietly blames the wrong mod. An honest gap is better than a confident wrong answer, so the report says so plainly instead of showing numbers it cannot stand behind.

Frame cost, garbage collections and memory growth are measured directly, not estimated.

[size=4][b]Notes[/b][/size]
Reports are written in English even when the game is not, because the people who need to read them maintain the mods named in them.

Nothing here changes gameplay, balance or save data, and it is safe to add or remove at any time.

[size=4][b]Source and issues[/b][/size]
Source code, release notes and issue tracking are available on [url=https://github.com/AcTePuKc/travellers-rest-translation-mod]GitHub[/url].
